* ''The catalog splits by face'' (operator, 2026-11-06, approving the house's defaults). No vessel-wide content key stands: each face holds its own catalog (`D`, sealed under the face), and a floor catalog names public bags alone (`F`); the daemon bag splits into the floor core (`F`, signed) and each face's daemon wiki content (`D`). The floor catalog's fields stand enumerated: a public bag's id, its kind and its published lookup reference, nothing else, so no private bag's name or metadata reaches `F`. The sealed-store carrier holds it, carried by the b1 lanes' carriers at their land.

